agent-ops task task-6f2ce01d-50d3-4746-ba27-a26ec2eab4dd: Criteria advisory reruns once after a substantive revise
intent: Add optional report trigger create|rerun|revise. Core = criteriaSnapshot without surface; stale and due compare the redacted core with the stored snapshot core. Due when a report exists, its trigger is not revise, and the core changed. task revise runs it blocking via a hook wired in bin.ts like onTaskCreated. Replace the no-auto-rerun rule in spec en/zh, README, managed guidance, run instruction and render text.
criteria:
- revise-rerun-once: After task revise changes criteria, intent, goal or assigned scope of a task whose current advisory report exists and was not revise-triggered, exactly one blocking advisory round runs with trigger revise and its advice is shown in the revise output (text and --json data.criteriaReview, as for task create); a second such revise, a surface-only revise, a same-criteria revise, and a task with no advisory report run none and show the existing advisory status; an explicit --rerun makes the next substantive revise eligible again. The revision is saved before the round: an advisory NOT_RUN still returns TASK_REVISED with the NOT_RUN advice, and cancellation returns CRITERIA_REVIEW_CANCELLED with the revision kept. Tests in tests/review/criteria.test.ts cover each.
- core-staleness: The advisory view is stale only when criteria, intent, goal or assigned scope differ from the reviewed snapshot; a surface-only revision leaves it current; reports without trigger stay valid, and a report with an invalid trigger value is unreadable (status shows no advisory, as for any malformed report); tests cover each.
- guidance-text: Managed loop guidance (runtime/src/install/harness.ts and tests/install/profiles.test.ts), the advisory render text, the run worker instruction and README.md state the once-automatic rerun rule and no longer say revise never reruns; the full test suite passes.
- spec-docs: REVIEW-CRITERIA-001 in docs/en/spec/review.md and docs/zh-TW/spec/review.md describes the once-automatic rerun and core staleness (positive and negative examples updated), and CHANGELOG.md has an Unreleased entry.
